WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
About 850 kilometres north of
Adelaide, in South Australia,

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.090
lies the opal-mining town of Coober Pedy.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.350
Opals were first found there in 1915.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.710
The State Library of South Australia
credits it with about 70 per cent of the

5
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.030
world's opal.

6
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.190
In 2021, 1,437 people lived there.

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.310
Many live in dugouts: homes
cut into the sandstone.

8
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.790
Why live underground?

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.590
To shelter from dust storms?

10
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.950
Because building land is scarce?

11
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.910
In this mission, you'll weigh the
challenges extreme places pose:

12
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.230
relief, climate, human
discomfort and remoteness.

13
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.850
Then you'll climb to La
Rinconada, in the Peruvian Andes,

14
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.110
about 5,100 metres up,
where the air is thin.

15
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.320
Your mission: explain why many Coober Pedy
residents live in homes dug into rock.
